# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check these out
# with CRLF endings. A shell script with CRLF fails on Linux with a confusing
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", and re-zipping from such a checkout
# would ship the breakage to the live ISO.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.nix text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf

*.zip binary
